## Commands Used

### Check SSH service

```bash
sudo systemctl status ssh
```

### Review SSH logs

```bash
sudo journalctl -u ssh
```

### Show successful and failed SSH authentication

```bash
sudo journalctl -u ssh | grep -E "Accepted|Failed"
```

### Show logged-in users

```bash
who
```

### Show active sessions

```bash
w
```

### Show network sockets and ports

```bash
ss
```

